WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.180
Does Moff Gideon finally get defeated? Will&nbsp;
Grogu at long last be promoted to Mandolorian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:10.980
apprentice? And what can we expect for season 4?&nbsp;
You've got questions about the season 3 ending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:15.960
of The Mandalorian. We've got answers.
 
For most of The Mandalorian Season 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:21.000
the endgame is clear. Finally, after multiple&nbsp;
seasons and decades of in-universe oppression&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.860
under the Empire, the Mandalorians are ready to&nbsp;
retake their home. At the beginning of the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:31.140
Din shows little interest in the idea of restoring&nbsp;
Mandalore, but that's fitting for the show. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:36.120
Din and Grogu are still central, Bo-Katan has&nbsp;
gradually become a co-star along with them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:40.320
By throwing her into the spotlight, Season 3&nbsp;
brings in storylines that have been running&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.580
since The Clone Wars. This history makes&nbsp;
the season finale all the more impactful.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:49.200
Thanks to a combined force of Bo-Katan's&nbsp;
old mercenaries, the Children of the Watch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:54.360
and a few Mandalorians who were abandoned&nbsp;
on Mandalore, Moff Gideon falls. His army&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:59.580
of stormtroopers cosplaying as Mandalorians is&nbsp;
defeated, as are his Elite Praetorian Guards.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:04.080
Amid the destruction of his base, the finale&nbsp;
offers hope for a bright future on Mandalore.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:09.420
The world's once lush landscape is glimpsed&nbsp;
in underground cave gardens. At long last,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:13.140
the clans are united in a glorious&nbsp;
mission to heal, not to conquer.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:17.220
For Bo-Katan, rebuilding a society&nbsp;
that's been devastated by eons of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:21.780
war is definitely not going to be easy. But&nbsp;
it truly feels like the Mandalorians can do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:25.860
it this time — they can forge a new future&nbsp;
for themselves and their descendants.  
 &nbsp;

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:31.200
Moff Gideon's delusional self-importance has&nbsp;
stood in opposition to the Mandalorian people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.900
since Season 1. He's the ultimate colonialist:&nbsp;
a man so infatuated with the idea of empire that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:41.340
he dresses up in a store-bought Darth Vader&nbsp;
Halloween costume to make himself feel tall.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:46.440
We've known since Season 1 that Mandalore was a&nbsp;
pet project for Gideon. We know that he fancies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:51.360
himself a superior version of the Mandalorian&nbsp;
warrior, even though his only maxed-out skills&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.100
are monologuing and Zoom calls. By the&nbsp;
end of The Mandalorian Season 3, Gideon's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.100 --> 00:02:00.660
delusions of grandeur catch up to him — but not&nbsp;
before he makes an absolute fool of himself.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.680
"Mandalorians are weak, once&nbsp;
they lose their trinkets."

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:09.180
Creating an army of Force-sensitive super&nbsp;
soldiers equipped with Mandalorian weaponry?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:14.700
Not a bad plan. But when you use yourself — a&nbsp;
middle-aged middle manager, in Gideon's case — as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:19.680
the template, it starts to fall apart. Where&nbsp;
Palpatine represents the power-hungry evil of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.960
empire and Vader represents those it corrupts,&nbsp;
Gideon represents the sad, desperate rubes who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:30.060
sell their souls for a lie of significance. In&nbsp;
short, Gideon embodies the myth that colonial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:35.220
empire sells to its agents: that you are both&nbsp;
capable and deserving of becoming an emperor unto&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:40.500
yourself if you stand on the shoulders of someone&nbsp;
else's culture. So, it's apt, then, that Gideon's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:45.720
world comes crashing down on him, manifested in&nbsp;
the form of a flaming Imperial light cruiser.  
 &nbsp;

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:50.640
The Mandalorians are stronger than Gideon&nbsp;
and his stormtroopers. They're more skilled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.420
better trained, and more dedicated.&nbsp;
These facts have never been in doubt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:59.880
but they also haven't led to many wins in the&nbsp;
past. The Empire has numbers, money, and beskar.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:04.680
Bo-Katan leads her united Mandalorian&nbsp;
front to victory at the end of Season 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:09.240
and it's that unity that's the key. All&nbsp;
the skill and knee rockets in the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:13.020
won't prevail if infighting persists.&nbsp;
At least, that's the message that The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:18.060
Mandalorian tries to drive home. Bo says&nbsp;
it herself while facing off against Gideon:

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.702
"Mandalorians are stronger together."

00:03:20.702 --> 00:03:23.700
This isn't just a commentary on&nbsp;
their past division in the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:28.320
but across all of the Star Wars canon.&nbsp;
Dave Filoni's modern Mandalorian saga&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:33.360
began in January of 2010 with the Clone Wars&nbsp;
episode "The Mandalore Plot." If you've been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:38.160
following the story since then, it's been a long&nbsp;
journey. Civil wars led to a peaceful government,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.900
which was dismantled by terrorist attacks and&nbsp;
political corruption. The planet was taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:47.340
over by crime syndicates and renegade Sith,&nbsp;
then thrown under the fist of the Empire.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:51.600
For so long, the Mandalorians have battled&nbsp;
one another and suffered the consequences.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:55.920
But in the Mandalorian Season 3 finale,&nbsp;
it's their cooperation and shared vision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:00.660
that ultimately leads them to victory. Even&nbsp;
in the final duel against Moff Gideon himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:06.540
it takes the combined efforts of Bo-Katan, Din,&nbsp;
and Grogu to finish him off. That's not a mark&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:10.980
of Gideon's superior power, but rather&nbsp;
a mark of just how strong unity can be.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:16.260
Since Star Wars: The Clone Wars, the Darksaber&nbsp;
has been at the center of the Mandalorian story.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:21.180
Only a successful fight to the death can earn&nbsp;
someone the ancient weapon, and only its power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:25.920
can unite the clans ... according to some. In&nbsp;
reality, the black blade has been more of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:31.080
curse since it was introduced in The Clone Wars.&nbsp;
Darth Maul uses it to kill Duchess Satine Kryze,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:35.940
Moff Gideon uses it to oppress the Mandalorian&nbsp;
people, and Bo-Katan's lack of claim to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:39.840
sword erodes her reputation with her&nbsp;
followers. So maybe it's for the best,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:44.100
and a little bit fitting, that the Darksaber is&nbsp;
destroyed in the climactic battle with Gideon.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:49.260
Perhaps, as Bo-Katan has repeatedly suggested,&nbsp;
rules that force Mandalorians to kill each other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:53.520
aren't rules worth following. Perhaps the&nbsp;
Darksaber didn't represent the strength of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:58.320
Mandalore, but the weakness of its people's&nbsp;
unending desire for bloodshed. By destroying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:02.700
the weapon, Gideon may have actually set&nbsp;
the Mandalorians free. It's a new era&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.780
now — one where the possession of an ancient&nbsp;
relic won't determine who's fit to rule.
 &nbsp;

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:11.580
Watching Grogu learn more about himself and&nbsp;
the galaxy has always been a high point of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:16.080
The Mandalorian. He demonstrates just how far&nbsp;
he's come in the final battle on Mandalore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:21.600
in which he saves Din from stormtroopers, fends&nbsp;
off three Praetorian Guards, helps Bo-Katan defeat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:26.880
Moff Gideon, and protects the whole squad from a&nbsp;
massive explosion. His Force shield technique is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:31.200
particularly striking because it echoes the&nbsp;
end of The Mandalorian Season 1. Back then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:35.040
it took all of Grogu's might just&nbsp;
to stop a single flametrooper. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:38.820
he can hold back the fires of a crashing&nbsp;
star cruiser. It's only fitting, then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:42.840
that Season 3 ends with Grogu promoted&nbsp;
from foundling to Mandalorian apprentice.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:50.204
"Grogu is my apprentice. He's no longer&nbsp;
a foundling. Add him to the Song."

00:05:50.204 --> 00:05:53.580
And with that advancement in rank comes&nbsp;
an even more important development:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.580 --> 00:06:00.000
being officially adopted by Din Djarin and taking&nbsp;
on the name Din Grogu. It's sweet, satisfying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.860
and bound to give you a lump in the throat.  
 
At the end of the Mandalorian Season 3 finale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:09.900
Din tells New Republic Ranger Carson Teva&nbsp;
that he wants a more reputable line of work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:14.040
now that he's a father. He proposes working as&nbsp;
a freelance contractor for the New Republic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.580
which would definitely be a step&nbsp;
up from ordinary bounty hunting.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:21.540
With this new job under his belt and&nbsp;
a cute little house to raise Grogu in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:27.180
Din has really come full circle. We first meet him&nbsp;
in Season 1 running dangerous missions on Nevarro.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:32.640
The planet is a wretched hive of scum, villainy,&nbsp;
and Imperial holdouts, and the Mandalorians live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:36.600
in the sewers. Now, at the end of Season&nbsp;
3, Din is living on the same planet, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:40.920
things are quite different. His work has helped&nbsp;
transform Nevarro into a thriving trade hub,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:45.720
and he has an official sanction from the galactic&nbsp;
government to suss out and put away bad guys.
 &nbsp;

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:49.560
If there is one prevailing theme&nbsp;
in The Mandalorian Season 3,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:53.580
it's summed up midway through the finale.&nbsp;
The captain of the survivors who've been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:58.200
living on Mandalore leads Bo-Katan and her&nbsp;
crew to a safe haven — a cave teeming with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:02.460
wildlife. He tells Bo that they have been&nbsp;
planting farms to restore the ecosystem,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:07.800
and when she asks how such a thing is possible on&nbsp;
a barren planet, he responds that life persists.

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:12.360
The sentiment worked in Jurassic Park, and it&nbsp;
works here, too. No matter how powerful evil may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:16.860
become, the natural balance of the universe&nbsp;
will always find a way to fight back. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:22.440
theme underscores most of the season. Bo-Katan is&nbsp;
alone and hopeless at the start after losing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:28.080
Darksaber and her forces. But by reconnecting with&nbsp;
her heritage, she finds new hope. Nevarro manages&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:32.700
to become a peaceful world despite decades&nbsp;
of Outer Rim chaos and Imperial violence. 
 &nbsp;

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:38.280
The first two seasons of The Mandalorian focus&nbsp;
squarely on Din's adventures. Most of the action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:42.780
takes place in the Outer Rim or the Mid Rim,&nbsp;
and a handful of New Republic rangers are the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:47.700
only glimpse of core galactic society. All&nbsp;
that changes in Season 3. We get an entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:52.500
episode on Coruscant, numerous deep dives&nbsp;
into the nature of post-Imperial politics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:56.340
and a look behind the curtain at Grand&nbsp;
Admiral Thrawn's impending return.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:08:01.920
One message prevails through all of this: The&nbsp;
New Republic isn't half as safe or secure as it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:06.300
would like to think. The amnesty program,&nbsp;
meant to rehabilitate former Imperials,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:11.280
is full of holes, allowing for people like Elia&nbsp;
Kane to gain New Republic access while still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:16.080
working for the Empire. The Outer Rim is far too&nbsp;
large for the government to police or protect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:20.280
and the so-called Shadow Council&nbsp;
remains active in, well, the shadows.

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:25.500
All of this helps explain the rise of the First&nbsp;
Order in the sequel trilogy. It might have seemed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:29.340
strange and even rushed in The Force Awakens&nbsp;
when the First Order appeared on the scene and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:34.200
quickly destroyed half a dozen planets. But&nbsp;
now, we see just how much careful scheming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:40.500
and New Republic inefficacy led to that moment.  
 
While the New Republic struggles and the Imperial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:46.020
Remnant schemes, the rest of the galaxy seems&nbsp;
to be thriving. The Mandalorian Season 3 seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:49.980
to argue that grassroots community projects,&nbsp;
not massive governments, are the way forward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:54.300
especially in the Outer Rim and the Mid&nbsp;
Rim. Nevarro is the best example of this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:58.440
turning saloons into schoolhouses and&nbsp;
dangerous environments into hospitable homes.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:03.480
An often-overlooked aspect of the Star Wars&nbsp;
story is that the Republic truly was corrupt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:07.980
by the time Palpatine toppled it. The Senate&nbsp;
failed to serve its constituents, the galactic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:13.200
core hoarded the riches of the galaxy, and there&nbsp;
was rampant corruption. These ideas are alluded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:18.120
to in the prequels, but they're even clearer in&nbsp;
The Clone Wars. The Mandalorian Season 3 suggests&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:22.500
that the New Republic isn't really much better.&nbsp;
The galaxy is certainly improving now that it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:26.940
out from under Palpatine's thumb, but it's the&nbsp;
regular people fighting for their own localities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:31.320
not the bigwigs on Coruscant, who make&nbsp;
the difference. As the old Mandalorian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:35.160
captain says of the plants on Mandalore,&nbsp;
all they need to thrive is room to grow.

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:39.900
After retaking Mandalore, defeating Moff&nbsp;
Gideon, and officially becoming a family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:44.520
Din and Grogu have earned some time off&nbsp;
at their new home on Nevarro. But The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:48.780
Mandalorian Season 4 is coming, and we already&nbsp;
have some clues as to what it might hold.

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:52.860
Gideon may be gone, but the Imperial&nbsp;
Remnant is still building strength in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:57.240
the far reaches of space. Grand Admiral&nbsp;
Thrawn is set to return in Ahsoka,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:01.500
and his campaign against the New Republic&nbsp;
could spill into Season 4. Now that Din is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:05.400
a contractor for the galactic government, he&nbsp;
could be called into action against Thrawn.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:10.320
And since Dave Filoni is now making a Star Wars&nbsp;
movie to wrap up the so-called "Mandoverse" saga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:13.800
it's likely that the shows will&nbsp;
continue to overlap in big ways.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:18.780
As for Mandalore itself, things look bright.&nbsp;
The Armorer tells Din at the end of Season 3&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:22.920
that he must take Grogu on adventures now that&nbsp;
he's his apprentice, which will likely keep the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:28.500
pair away from the homeworld for a while. A fresh&nbsp;
run of episodic voyages likely awaits in Season 4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:32.880
but we'll probably still get some visits&nbsp;
to Bo-Katan's reconstruction efforts. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:37.860
bigger question now isn't what The Mandalorian&nbsp;
Season 4 will hold, but when it will arrive.

